cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "lean-ordinal-analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sabean"
    given-names: "Steven"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9238-610X"
version: "0.3.0"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SteveWmoc/lean-ordinal-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/SteveWmoc/lean-ordinal-analysis"
abstract: >-
  Executable recursive ordinal notation systems in Lean 4. Version 0.3.0
  extracts a reusable verified ordinal-notation API from the completed
  epsilon-zero development. The library provides exact initial-segment
  certification, generic zero/successor/limit classifiers, and certified
  limit sequences with monotonicity, boundedness, cofinality, and semantic
  convergence. The epsilon-zero implementation is packaged as a reference
  instance of the generic interfaces.
keywords:
  - "ordinal analysis"
  - "proof theory"
  - "ordinal notation"
  - "epsilon zero"
  - "fundamental sequences"
  - "order isomorphism"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "mathlib"
  - "formal verification"
